; RockCluster1 — one of 4 Rock terrain cluster variants (D-42 model_scenes variety pass).
; Composes already-imported pieces (no new download): 2x Rock_1 (Ultimate Nature Pack,
; project/assets/terrain/rock_1/Rock_1.fbx) + 1x Rock_Moss_3 (same pack, already imported
; for the Den prop at project/assets/props/den/Rock_Moss_3.fbx) — reused here as a THIRD,
; distinct rock piece, not duplicated content.
;
; WHY A CLUSTER, NOT ONE BIG ROCK: the prior single-variant Rock1.tscn used Rock_1 at
; NATURAL SCALE (height 0.87775 — nearly tile-height), which read in-engine as "one giant
; rock," not "a bunch of rocks" (explicit human complaint). This variant instead scatters
; SEVERAL SMALL rocks, each scaled well below natural size:
;   - Rock_1 raw measured AABB: footprint 0.485x0.467, height 0.877 (matches Rock1.tscn's
;     own header). Scaled here to 0.22-0.28 (target height ~0.19-0.25 tile-units).
;   - Rock_Moss_3 raw measured AABB: footprint 0.738x0.803, height 0.557 (measured fresh
;     for this pass — Den.tscn uses its own separate scale, not reused here). Scaled to
;     0.40 (target height ~0.22).
; All 3 pieces land well under the OLD single-rock height (0.877) — FLAG FOR HUMAN
; SIGN-OFF: the exact per-piece scale/spacing is a first-pass judgment call, not measured
; against any GDD number (none exists for rock height).
;
; Slab matches the existing Rock terrain grey (Color(0.55, 0.55, 0.58, 1)), same geometry
; as Rock1.tscn's slab, for tonal consistency across all rock-cluster variants.
;
; SLAB WIDENED 0.94 -> 1.0 (2026-08-16, human-reported cross-tile seam gap): matches
; `WorldGrid.TILE_SIZE` exactly so adjacent tile slabs' edges touch with no sky-blue gap —
; same fix, same exact-1.0-match approach as CommonTree1.tscn; see that scene's header for
; the full explanation. X/Z only, Y (0.2) untouched.
